{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He has sworn, you are a priest</b> — every king serves, and likewise \"the sons of David were priests.\" The meaning: to serve HaShem. And the meaning is that Israel will wage war and you will take the tithe, just as Melchizedek took from Abraham. And the yod of <b>דברתי</b> is superfluous, and the meaning is upon their customary practice, like <b>דוברות בים</b>; or the letter kaf is missing: <b>אתה כהן לעולם על דברת</b>, like <b>על דבר</b>, that you are like Melchizedek, about whom it is written: \"and he was a priest to El Elyon.\" And the word <b>אתה</b> is on account of something else. And Rabbi Moses said: because you are a king of justice, like: \"and David administered justice and righteousness to all his people.\" The meaning: it is much for you to fight, for HaShem supports your right hand and strikes kings through you on the day of His wrath."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 110, :notes {0 "The comment 'every king serves' interprets כהן as one who serves/ministers; the prooftext 'the sons of David were priests' alludes to 2 Samuel 8:18. The verse fragments cited without explicit references are from Genesis 14:18, 2 Samuel 8:15, and language echoing Psalms 110:5-6."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:25.285123805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}